只输出严格JSON，恰好包含id（metadata.id原样）、summary_zh（15到140个Unicode字符，通常40到100字）、category（枚举）、tags（2到5个不重复关键词，每个最多30字符）、confidence（0到1，仅自评）、insufficient_evidence（布尔）、evidence（1到3个对象，每个恰好包含paragraph_id、fact）、limitations（0到5个字符串）。只选择输入中长度20至120字符的完整片段编号；fact是该片段支持的中文事实转述。不要输出quote，不要自行抄写、拼接、删改或补造引用。程序会按编号附上原文。一个编号只用一次；最多3条证据。不得增加字段。
摘要和limitations保留会改变功能意义的前提、平台例外和限制：设密码后才认证、页面保持打开才提醒、依赖外部组件、估算不等于保证。只写已实现功能，不将规划当完成。证据不足就标记，不编造。
图像识别/分类不是媒体创作，没有贴切类别归other；量化、计算与领域研究归search-research，不因多智能体实现归agents-automation；模型/CLI适配与插件开发工具归coding-development；市场/精选目录按搜索发现归search-research。不要按附属同步、备份或评论功能分类。不要推断本机客户端等于本地模型。
摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Tavily-backed web search for DeepSeek Harness: multi-key pool with balance-aware rotation, automatic failover, and usage stats — switchable from the DSH settings panel.","id":"gh:1376144026","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-tavily-pool","slug":"stormbuf/dsh-tavily-pool","topics":["deepseek","dsh","dsh-plugin","tavily","web-search"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Tavily-backed web search for DeepSeek Harness: multi-key pool with balance-aware rotation, automatic"},{"id":"p1s2","text":" failover, and usage stats — switchable from the DSH settings panel."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-tavily-pool"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"**English** | 简体中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"Tavily-backed web search **and** page fetching for DeepSeek Harness: multi-key pool with balance-awa"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"re rotation, automatic failover, cooldown, official `/usage` balance reporting, and independent togg"},{"id":"p4s3","text":"les for search and fetch — configurable from the DSH settings panel."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"> Not to be confused with `SZMY-haruhi/dsh-tavily` (single key / keyless, no scheduling) or `@yuuz12"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"/dsh-tavily` (multi-key, but no fetch takeover and it rewrites internal fields at runtime). This plu"},{"id":"p5s3","text":"gin manages a **pool** of keys, schedules by remaining balance, and takes over **both** `web_search`"},{"id":"p5s4","text":"ool** of keys, schedules by remaining balance, and takes over **both** `web_search` and `web_fetch`."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## Features"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"- **Multi-key pool** — add one key or paste a whole batch (one per line), label, enable/disable, reo"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"rder, remove one or several at once; the UI only ever shows masked keys\n- **Scheduling policy** — sw"},{"id":"p7s3","text":"itch between balance-first ordering and plain manual order, where the list order becomes the schedul"},{"id":"p7s4","text":"ing order\n- **Balance-aware rotation** — highest remaining balance first; three-state balance (the l"},{"id":"p7s5","text":"imit comes from `key.limit`, falling back to the account's `account.plan_limit` — only when **both**"},{"id":"p7s6","text":" are explicitly `null` is a key unlimited and ranked first; unknown goes last)\n- **Automatic failove"},{"id":"p7s7","text":"r** — a failing key hands the request to the next one\n- **Cooldown** — honors upstream `Retry-After`"},{"id":"p7s8","text":"; cooled keys are hard-excluded until it expires, and when every key is cooling the request waits fo"},{"id":"p7s9","text":"r the earliest one within a bounded budget\n- **Status-aware errors** — separates temporary failures,"},{"id":"p7s10","text":" permanent key death (body-inspected, never status-code-only), and quota exhaustion (`432` / `433` t"},{"id":"p7s11","text":"reated alike: the key stays out of rotation until `/usage` confirms a positive balance)\n- **Official"},{"id":"p7s12","text":" balance, refreshed on use** — the card's credit figure is the official `/usage` reading (limit − us"},{"id":"p7s13","text":"ed). A reading is pulled again when the key being used has one over an hour old, when a key is added"},{"id":"p7s14","text":", and for any key still missing a reading the next time the plugin is used at all. The plugin keeps "},{"id":"p7s15","text":"**no** credit accounting of its own: Tavily's billing rules can change at any time, so a locally com"},{"id":"p7s16","text":"puted figure could silently become wrong. Between readings the ordering is nudged forward by a delib"},{"id":"p7s17","text":"erately rough per-call estimate that is never shown as a number of its own; it does move the display"},{"id":"p7s18","text":"ed `used` figure, so the card also says how old the last official reading is. Nothing runs in the ba"},{"id":"p7s19","text":"ckground: no search or fetch means no `/usage` traffic at all\n- **Balance refresh** — pulls official"},{"id":"p7s20","text":" `/usage` with per-key sliding-window quota reservation, so it never trips the 10-per-10-minutes lim"},{"id":"p7s21","text":"it\n- **Configurable search parameters** — search depth, result cap, topic, and generated-answer togg"},{"id":"p7s22","text":"le, all taking effect immediately\n- **Fetch takeover (off by default)** — maps `web_fetch` to Tavily"},{"id":"p7s23","text":" `/extract`, returning plain text (never HTML, which DSH would convert a second time); extraction de"},{"id":"p7s24","text":"pth and output format are configurable. Turn it on in settings when you want Tavily to handle fetchi"},{"id":"p7s25","text":"ng too\n- **Call history and chart** — every call is recorded (key, endpoint, outcome, duration, `req"},{"id":"p7s26","text":"uest_id`) and drawn as a 14-day call-count chart; the file is bounded by both an entry cap and a 30-"},{"id":"p7s27","text":"day window\n- **Independent toggles** — search and fetch can be switched back to the official provide"},{"id":"p7s28","text":"rs separately\n- **Zero runtime dependencies** — plain ESM, no build step"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"> **Shipped:** the whole spec — search takeover and its toggle, the key pool (single key,\n> pasted b"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"atch, bulk removal), failover with cooldown, search parameters, the scheduling\n> policy, balance ref"},{"id":"p8s3","text":"resh, fetch takeover with its own toggle (off by default), call history\n> with its chart, the per-ke"},{"id":"p8s4","text":"y call stats and balance bar, the connectivity test, and the\n> settings card with its HTTP API."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"From the npm registry:"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"Or straight from GitHub, which needs no registry account. Pin a released tag when you want a\nreprodu"},{"id":"p12s2","text":"cible version — see the tags for\nthe ones that exist:"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"Both routes install the same files: the `files` whitelist in `package.json` applies to git installs "},{"id":"p14s2","text":"too, so no `test/` or `scripts/` directory comes along."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"Then restart DSH, open **Settings → Plugins → dsh-tavily-pool** and paste your Tavily API key(s). Ke"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"ys are entered through the panel only — the plugin does not read environment variables or the DSH cr"},{"id":"p15s3","text":"ough the panel only — the plugin does not read environment variables or the DSH credentials service."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"See `docs/usage.md` for configuration, scheduling behaviour, billing, and manual rollback steps."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"## Compatibility"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"DeepSeek Harness is in preview, so its architecture and plugin interfaces may change between release"},{"id":"p18s2","text":"s. This plugin isolates nearly all host-specific knowledge in one thin adapter layer (`lib/dsh/`), p"},{"id":"p18s3","text":"lus the zero-build client half (`lib/client.js`) and the provider pin in `cordis.patch.yml`, and pro"},{"id":"p18s4","text":"bes host capabilities at load time, so that adapting to a breaking change stays cheap."},{"id":"p19s1","text":"**Tested against DSH `0.1.7-rc.2`.** A newer release may still need re-adaptation; the plugin probes"},{"id":"p19s2","text":" host capabilities at load time and reports a clear error naming the missing one rather than failing"},{"id":"p19s3","text":" silently. Its host peer ranges carry **only a lower bound**, so an untested DSH release never refus"},{"id":"p19s4","text":"es to load the plugin — DSH 0.1.7 added a hard gate that skips a whole bundle whose peer range exclu"},{"id":"p19s5","text":"des the running version, which turns a stale upper bound into a silently missing plugin. The step-by"},{"id":"p19s6","text":"-step checklist lives in `docs/dsh-upgrade.md`."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"Installing through `dsh plugin add` makes this package a **bundle layer** of the target profile (it "},{"id":"p20s2","text":"lands in that profile's `dsh.profile.bundles`, after the DSH bundles), which is what lets its `cordi"},{"id":"p20s3","text":"s.patch.yml` pin the providers. Your own profile patch is applied after every bundle layer, so it ca"},{"id":"p20s4","text":"n always override or disable what this plugin does — see Manual rollback."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"## License"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"MIT"}],"truncated":false}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
